    affiliation: INESC TEC, Porto, Portugal
repository-code: https://github.com/davidecarneiro/ai-act-compliance-ledger
abstract: >-
  A compliance-as-code architecture that turns EU AI Act obligations for
  high-risk AI systems into third-party-verifiable evidence records: a
  Compliance Policy Engine with fail-closed validation, Ed25519-signed and
  hash-chained records (RFC 8785 canonical form), OSCAL 1.1.2 assessment
  results with selective disclosure, and per-record or batched anchoring on
  Hyperledger Fabric. Includes the credit-scoring and MultiFlow cases, the
  pre-registered experiment protocols, every result file and the scripts that
  draw the figures. Branch `article`; the dissertation's version is the tag
  `thesis-v1.0`.
keywords:
  - EU AI Act
  - compliance-as-code
  - tamper-evident logging
  - OSCAL
  - Hyperledger Fabric
  - MLOps
  - selective disclosure
references:
